      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3383246672625664
    m_Localized: 'Hold on, traveler. This world isn''t as I remember it: ever since
      my travel companion pushed further to explore it, everything seems to follow
      its own silent rules, rules no one explains. You only learn them by observing.


      Observe
      the creatures you meet, collect what you find along the way: they''re the only
      clues you''ll need to overcome the obstacles ahead.


      Press TAB to check
      your notebook. It updates on its own every time you observe a new species or
      collect something. When you face an obstacle, press E: if you''ve collected
      what''s needed, you''ll be able to compose a creature able to overcome it.


      Hold
      Shift to run, when the road ahead is long.


      Go on, and keep your eyes
      open.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3384503630036992
    m_Localized: 'Look over there, the lizards. Watch them closely: they''re a joy
      to see swim.


      But don''t think they''re all the same. Some dart through
      the water with no effort at all, others swim more calmly, and I''ve even seen
      a few that just float there, still, as if they''d forgotten how it''s done.
      Same species, yet each one in its own way.


      Watch them carefully: you''ll
      find them in your notebook now.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3385483536891904
    m_Localized: 'Look up there, the fairies. Watch them closely: they''re a marvel
      to see fly.


      But they''re not all the same either. Some dart through
      the air fast as the wind, others fly more calmly, and I''ve even seen a few
      that just hover in place, as if they''d forgotten where they were going. Same
      species, yet each one in its own way.


      Watch them carefully: you''ll
      find them in your notebook now.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3386805808005120
    m_Localized: 'Look at that one, over there. It''s neither fish nor bird: it swims
      and flies, both at once, the same creature.


      You won''t see many like
      it. But if you ever come across a stretch where water and empty air follow
      one another with no solid ground in between, you''ll understand why they come
      in handy: you won''t need to switch creatures every few steps, one alone will
      see you through, capable of both from start to finish.


      Watch it carefully:
      you''ll find it in your notebook now.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3387202555609088
    m_Localized: 'You''ve come this far. You''ve watched different creatures, one
      by one, taking your time. You found capabilities and behaviors apart from each
      other, scattered across the world, and it was you who brought them together,
      again and again, to build the right creature for each obstacle. And when an
      obstacle left no way around it, you understood that all it took was a single
      creature capable of more than one thing at once.


      You didn''t just collect
      pieces: you put them together yourself, differently each time.


      If you
      go on, you''ll return to the start of the map, but you''ll carry with you everything
      you''ve learned. You''ll be able to keep exploring the areas you haven''t visited
      yet, if there are any left.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3389942509862912
    m_Localized: Seleziona italiano
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3399791348023296
    m_Localized: Press E to talk
